Get_Corner_Positions @0x43ca40 copies the car FD lane byte into the eight
corner FD records. Original 0x43ca8e loads BYTE [car*44+0x7926ba]; the eight
A2 stores at 0x43ca98..0x43cabb write exactly one byte to 0x79263e, 0x792612,
0x7925e6, 0x7925ba, 0x79258e, 0x792562, 0x792536 and 0x79250a.

The Ghidra symbols were incorrectly int lvalues. In particular, the four-byte
store at 0x79263e clears the low two bytes of grounded_count[0] @0x792640.
FUN_00440ab0 can therefore never reach its original 100-step recovery timer
while the car is grounded and Get_Corner_Positions runs. Under complete
original history [9,7,3,7], L10 car0 incorrectly remains in mode5 after cf138,
where the original has recovered to mode0. Physical divergence precedes the
Setup_Debris RNG mismatch at cf151/t302. The same timer explains the earlier
L8 car0 divergence at cf162. Restore all eight literal BYTE field widths;
no engine state or recovery threshold is synthesized from the reference.

